  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CHACO JAGUAR CONSERVATION PROJECT</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Expanding our participatory network of private landowners and impact through the installation of new non-lethal, solar-powered electric conflict deterrent fences; inventories and mapping of current and prospective participatory stakeholder properties to incentivize the establishment of legal private reserves and evaluate potential to restore habitat; hosting the first series of human-jaguar conflict mitigation workshops in cooperation with regional livestock associations and in the most affected rural areas engaging local youth and communities through a series of presentations and discussions at rural schools, and hosting and running the first consumer focus groups to develop and refine market strategies for a sustainable supply chain.</narrative>
  </description>
